The registers of swe-muscl.m's GPU process kernel, merk_place, with all it
calls, from its image's assembly; no GPU is needed (docs/INPROGRESS.md,
Register pressure in GPU processes, steps 1 and 2). The column after the
SGPRs' is the scratch, then the waves a SIMD. A change in the waves or a
return of AGPRs shows here, not first as a slower step.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-registered-target

On gfx90a the default budget, 2 waves, keeps the VGPRs to a SIMD's half of
the register file, with no AGPRs. 4 waves, HIP's for its step, halve them.
On gfx1030, with no budget by default, the backend takes 4.
RUN: %gpu-registers --arch gfx90a --arch gfx1030 --top 0 %S/../../benchmarks/swe-muscl/swe-muscl.m | FileCheck %s
RUN: %gpu-registers --arch gfx90a --top 0 --merkc-flags="-O2 -fopenmp -fopenmp-version=61 -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations -fgpu-process-waves=4" %S/../../benchmarks/swe-muscl/swe-muscl.m | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=W4

CHECK:      == GPU processes, gfx1030:
CHECK-NEXT: Kernel VGPR AGPR SGPR Scratch Waves Spills Reloads
CHECK-NEXT: merk_place {{[0-9]+}} 0 {{[0-9]+}} {{[0-9]+}} 4 {{[0-9]+}} {{[0-9]+}}{{$}}
CHECK:      == GPU processes, gfx90a:
CHECK-NEXT: Kernel
CHECK-NEXT: merk_place {{2[0-9][0-9]}} 0 {{[0-9]+}} {{[0-9]+}} 2 {{[0-9]+}} {{[0-9]+}}{{$}}

W4:      == GPU processes, gfx90a:
W4-NEXT: Kernel
W4-NEXT: merk_place 128 0 {{[0-9]+}} {{[0-9]+}} 4 {{[0-9]+}} {{[0-9]+}}{{$}}
